# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Team Praise · VoltRelay hackathon repo
# Keeps: code (analysis/, src/, deck/), docs/, deliverables/, outputs/ (figures, tables, findings),
#        working/report (report sources).
# Drops: the dataset and derived data (too large for GitHub; the notebook re-downloads it from the
#        organisers' Google Drive folder), build artefacts, local tooling, caches.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dataset (836 MB raw CSVs) and derived Parquet (events.parquet alone is 228 MB > GitHub's 100 MB limit)
Hackathon Data Set _ Gradient/
data/
*.csv.gz

# Deck build artefacts
deck/node_modules/
deck/out/
deck/.render.lock

# Draft renders, superseded drafts and regenerable build intermediates
working/deck_png/
working/deck_contact_sheet.png
working/old_deck_v1/
working/ai_voice_backup/
working/report/*.html

# Local tooling (installed skills, editor/agent state, private Jupyter kernel)
.claude/
.agents/
.playwright-mcp/
.nbkernel/
skills-lock.json

# Logs and scratch output
*.log
outputs/notebook_build.log
outputs/profile_raw.txt

# Python / Jupyter / OS noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*
deck
# Your recorded video: a 3-minute 1080p export is usually 20-80 MB and is fine to commit. GitHub rejects files over
# 100 MB; if yours is larger, share it via Drive/YouTube instead and uncomment the next line.
# deliverables/3_Video/*.mp4
